Rauch comparison: the proof uses monotoneOn_of_deriv_nonneg on Icc 0 t, with `hx` from interior_Icc... wait, they apply `monotoneOn_of_deriv_nonneg` which requires the derivative to be nonnegative on the interior of the set? Let me check mathlib's `monotoneOn_of_deriv_nonneg`: its hypotheses are (convex : Convex ℝ s) (cont : ContinuousOn f s) (diff : DifferentiableOn ℝ f (interior s)) (h : ∀ x ∈ interior s, 0 ≤ deriv f x). Actually mathlib's `monotoneOn_of_deriv_nonneg` has `hdiff : DifferentiableOn ℝ f s` in newer versions. They pass differentiableOn over the whole set and the interior check for the derivative. Either way, they use `interior_Icc` to rewrite `hx : x ∈ interior (Icc 0 t)` into `0 < x ∧ x < t` — hmm, but `x ∈ interior (Icc 0 t)` gives `x ∈ Ioo 0 t` when 0 ≤ t. OK.

