/-- At the interior point `(0, T)` the probe function equals `-T`, and the principle gives
`-T ≤ 1` — the maximum is attained on the boundary, where the value `1` is taken. -/
theorem probe_interior {T : ℝ} (hT : 0 < T) : probeU (0, T) = -T := by
  change (0 : Fin 1 → ℝ) 0 - T = -T
  norm_num
```

